WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.940
So I recently set myself the challenge of finding the worst game on Steam.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.600
I do this on occasion just because I'm curious of what is actually at the bottom of the barrel and

00:00:10.059 --> 00:00:11.639
when I set out for this challenge

00:00:11.639 --> 00:00:16.679
I didn't want to just go looking for a game that was meant to be bad, because there are games like that all over the

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:21.329
place. They're made specifically to be bad and that can sometimes be funny,

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.269
but often time is just crap for the sake of being crap.

00:00:24.369 --> 00:00:26.909
What I wanted to find, was a game

00:00:27.099 --> 00:00:34.349
That had all the hope of being good and then despite the developers' best efforts turned out to be the worst.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:40.500
Thing. Ever. And there's different criteria for that. Number one, I wanted it to actually cost money

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.059
I wanted to actually spend money on this so I could be disappointed by the end result and number two

00:00:45.059 --> 00:00:51.659
I wanted something that kind of hit on a few different topics. It wasn't just game breakingly bad

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:55.709
No, I didn't want something that was super buggy, incredibly just crap.

00:00:55.709 --> 00:01:00.980
I wanted something that was actually in the gameplay itself

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.399
terrible 
(Mark gulps dramatically hard)

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:05.400
And I found it

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:07.440
I really found it.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:12.960
So the first victim of my search was a game called Drug Wars, and I actually came across some interesting -uh-

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.920
trivia behind this one. This was a hyped up game

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:22.660
But if you haven't heard of drug wars, you wouldn't be surprised. It wasn't originally called that. It was called

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:30.020
"Merchants of Brooklyn". It came out in 2009 and was this hyped up game that some people even pre-ordered apparently

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:32.020
But when it came out it was so

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:39.600
unbelievlably (sic) bad that they changed the name to try to appeal to something more and I couldn't even play it so I can't judge it

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:41.880
because the game wouldn't even load up for me

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:47.880
but some of the accompanying material and gameplay footage, which you'll find here in front of you

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.580
can showcase that it's not exactly the best game

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:54.460
the world, but by its Steam rating of 33% it's also not the worst.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.020
So I gave it a pass.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:00.640
The other game that I tried to play was called "Tunnel Rats". And this one was a

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:05.160
very low rated game on Steam like the other one at 34 percent,

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:09.560
but this one was about the gripping reality of the Vietnam War

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:17.100
showcasing a side of it that didn't work, but unfortunately after a brief opening segment, it didn't work as well

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:18.700
So I was left with

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:24.300
uh, another game on my list and I had a few more but I don't think I needed to go any farther.

